# Keep systemd from tracking backlight devices. Every brightness write makes
# the kernel send a backlight "change" uevent; Steam's idle dimming and the
# brightness slider send dozens a second. systemd updates the device unit for
# each one (and logs "Failed to enqueue SYSTEMD_WANTS job": SteamOS masks
# systemd-backlight@), which emits PropertiesChanged on D-Bus. Wine's
# mountmgr (winedevice.exe, running with every Proton game) re-reads the whole
# UDisks2 object tree on such signals, and with the ~130 UFS partitions that
# kept udisksd at up to ~90 % CPU and the little cores clocked up. Measured on
# the Retroid Pocket 6 while moving the slider: udisksd 34 % -> 4 %.
# Brightness is set through sysfs by gamescope/PowerDevil, not through systemd.
# Sorts after 99-systemd.rules, which adds the tag.
SUBSYSTEM=="backlight", TAG-="systemd"
